<p>The Participants text contains the sentence people skip: the Implementor interface "doesn't have to correspond exactly to Abstraction's interface; in fact the two interfaces can be quite different". <code>Window.drawRect()</code> is a <em>high-level</em> operation built from four calls to the <em>primitive</em> <code>devDrawLine()</code>. That is what makes Bridge different from "an interface with several implementations": the abstraction adds its own logic on top of the primitives. The running code is in lesson 4.C — the implementor side of the LabFlow example is:</p>
