<div class="callout">🧭 <strong>Apply it to LabFlow</strong> (illustration): when a reservation is cancelled, three things must happen — offer the slot to the waitlist, email the member, write an audit line. With Observer, <code>ReservationService</code> publishes one event and knows none of them. In Spring Boot this is built in: <code>ApplicationEventPublisher.publishEvent(new ReservationCancelled(…))</code> and an <code>@EventListener</code> method in each component.</div>
